    "narrative": "The landscape for today\u2019s slate is constrained by limited matchups, forcing us to lean on high-leverage veterans despite challenging opposing arms. **Bryce Harper** (Score: 49.40) anchors the lineup today; while he faces an elite opponent in Sale (xERA 2.79), **Bryce Harper** maintains the highest floor on the team. His premium spot in the #3 hole (+6% order advantage) and consistent xwOBA metrics keep him in \"Marginal\" start territory even against a top-tier southpaw. **Yainer Diaz** (Score: 44.28) follows in priority, benefiting from a favorable platoon split against Smith, H. While Smith\u2019s xERA of 3.07 is restrictive, the dynamic platoon advantage keeps **Yainer Diaz** viable as he occupies the #5 spot. **Braden Montgomery** (Score: 42.77) rounds out the active trio; his versatility as a switch hitter mitigates some of the risk against Blubaugh, though he remains a marginal play due to the production drop-off associated with the #7 spot in the order.\n\nThe bench decisions today were dictated largely by inactivity, as key contributors like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Lawrence Butler** are all unavailable due to scheduled off-days. **Justin Crawford** was the closest to cracking the starting lineup, but he ultimately fell victim to the platoon penalty against Sale and the optimizer\u2019s strict \"Not Starting\" exclusion. The remaining depth, including **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Kyle Karros**, were all sidelined to preserve our remaining game caps for higher-probability matchups. We are keeping a close watch on the weather and the finalization of the lineups for **Yainer Diaz** and **Braden Montgomery**, as any further shifts in their batting order could necessitate a late-scratch to protect our efficiency metrics.",
